  "markdown": "For professionals\n\n# Wallcovering support for your specification.\n\nChoose the route that fits your work. Bring the drawings, the material and the decisions still to be made.\n\nDesigners & architects\n\n## [Your specification. Considered down to the last return.](https://www.mrwallcover.com/professionals/designers/)\n\nBring the material, elevations and design intent together before installation begins. Pattern placement, natural panel variation and the junctions with joinery all deserve a decision before the first length is cut.\n\n![Setting out an Overture panel against a laser line.](https://www.mrwallcover.com/media/img/r/lee-broom-06-800.webp)\n\nSetting out an Overture panel to a laser line at the Lee Broom showroom, Shoreditch.Photograph: Dorin Burcus / Mr Wallcover.[See the Overture installation](https://www.mrwallcover.com/projects/calico-lee-broom-overture/)\n\n[Explore this service](https://www.mrwallcover.com/professionals/designers/)\n\nDevelopers & main contractors\n\n## [Wallcovering packages planned around the site.](https://www.mrwallcover.com/professionals/developers/)\n\nA reliable package starts with the scope and the sequence. Bring drawings, material delivery and wall readiness into the same conversation before booking the installation across rooms or floors.\n\n![Room at Brown's Hotel, Mayfair, during works: Adam's Eden wallcovering hung beneath an ornate plaster ceiling and chandelier, with protection board on the floor and a vacuum cleaner in view.](https://www.mrwallcover.com/media/img/browns-hotel-mayfair-07.jpg)\n\nBrown’s Hotel, Mayfair, during works: the wallcovering is hung while the floors remain protected.Mr Wallcover project photograph.[See the Brown’s Hotel package](https://www.mrwallcover.com/projects/browns-hotel-mayfair/)\n\n[Explore this service](https://www.mrwallcover.com/professionals/developers/)\n\nHotels & operators\n\n## [Considered finishes. A programme that respects the building.](https://www.mrwallcover.com/professionals/hotels/)\n\nA guest room, a corridor and a reception area have different demands. Plan the finish around how each space is used, how it is maintained and when it can be released for work.\n\n![Sample room at Hyde London City with a Timorous Beasties Tropical Clouded Leopard panel behind the bed.](https://www.mrwallcover.com/media/img/r/old-bailey-06-800.webp)\n\nThe sample room at Hyde London City: Tropical Clouded Leopard by Timorous Beasties, set out as a shaped headboard panel.Photograph: Dorin Burcus / Mr Wallcover.[See the Hyde London City programme](https://www.mrwallcover.com/projects/old-bailey-hotel/)\n\n[Explore this service](https://www.mrwallcover.com/professionals/hotels/)\n\nFit-out contractors\n\n## [The wallcovering package, run like part of your site team.](https://www.mrwallcover.com/professionals/fit-out-contractors/)\n\nMr Wallcover takes on the wallcovering package for fit-out main contractors. Risk assessments and method statements (RAMS) are issued for every package, Dorin Burcus personally supervises the site, and a core team of six wallpaper hangers and six decorators scales to 25–35 people on large projects.\n\n![The mural wrapped around an internal corner, full height.](https://www.mrwallcover.com/media/img/r/heathrow-05-800.webp)\n\nThe Calico Wallpaper mural continuing around an internal corner at Heathrow Terminal 4, installed overnight in a live terminal.Photograph: Dorin Burcus / Mr Wallcover.[View the Calico Wallpaper airside at Heathrow: a luxury fashion house's store, Terminal 4 case study](https://www.mrwallcover.com/projects/heathrow-terminal-4-calico/)\n\n[Explore this service](https://www.mrwallcover.com/professionals/fit-out-contractors/)\n\nAlready have a complete brief?\n\n## Send the work in front of you.\n\nA schedule, drawings and a short note are enough to begin. Include who is supplying the material and any date the tender needs.\n\n[Start a professional enquiry](https://www.mrwallcover.com/contact/?intent=install&audience=commercial)\n\nBy [Dorin Burcus](https://www.mrwallcover.com/about/#dorin), founder · Last reviewed 9 October 2026\n",
